{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Interactions.EmCouplingBarParity","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Interactions.EmCouplingBarParity","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.LinearCombination"],"declarations":12,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.emCouplingBare_not_bar_odd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.emCouplingBare_not_bar_odd","kind":"theorem","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/EmCouplingBarParity.lean#L128-L139","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.emCouplingBare_not_bar_even","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.emCouplingBare_not_bar_even","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/EmCouplingBarParity.lean#L117-L126","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.emAlphaSq_even_odd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.emAlphaSq_even_odd","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/EmCouplingBarParity.lean#L99-L107","doc":"The observable scale `α²` (the Hartree/Rydberg `q`-dependence)\ndecomposes with the doubled conjugate exponential `e^{−2λ}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.emAlpha_even_odd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.emAlpha_even_odd","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/EmCouplingBarParity.lean#L90-L97","doc":"`α` carries the **conjugate** exponential `e^{−λ}`: its bar-even part\nis the cosh multiple and its bar-odd part the *negative* sinh multiple of\nthe bar-invariant `B⁻¹` — opposite odd-part sign to the coupling. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.emAlpha_bar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.emAlpha_bar","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/EmCouplingBarParity.lean#L85-L88","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.emAlpha","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.emAlpha","kind":"def","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/EmCouplingBarParity.lean#L79-L83","doc":"The fine-structure object itself, `α = C(q)⁻¹`. The EM sector's\ncomparison observables (Coulomb energy, Hartree/Rydberg scale) carry their\n`q`-dependence through `α` and `α²`; the remaining factors are\n`q`-independent calibration constants. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.emCoupling_channel_ratio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.emCoupling_channel_ratio","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/EmCouplingBarParity.lean#L66-L75","doc":"The odd and even parts differ by the sinh/cosh factor pair: twice the\neven part is `(q+q⁻¹)·B`, twice the odd part is `(q−q⁻¹)·B`, whose ratio is\nthe `tanh` of the substrate rapidity (numerically ≈ 0.104 at the proton\npin — the probe's measured value). Stated multiplicatively to avoid a\ndivision hypothesis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.emCouplingBare_even_odd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.emCouplingBare_even_odd","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/EmCouplingBarParity.lean#L55-L64","doc":"**Exact bar decomposition of the EM coupling**: its even part is the\ncosh-channel multiple of the bar-invariant `B = [9]_q·[10]_q` and its odd\npart the sinh-channel multiple — the EM coupling is the full exponential\nmix, not a pure bar channel. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.emCouplingBare_bar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.emCouplingBare_bar","kind":"theorem","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/EmCouplingBarParity.lean#L49-L53","doc":"Bar image of the coupling: only the exponential prefactor moves. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.emCouplingBare","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.emCouplingBare","kind":"def","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/EmCouplingBarParity.lean#L46-L47","doc":"The bare electromagnetic coupling object `C(q) = q·[9]_q·[10]_q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.qint_bar_even","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.qint_bar_even","kind":"theorem","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/EmCouplingBarParity.lean#L40-L44","doc":"`[n]_q` is bar-even: invariant under `q ↦ q⁻¹`. No hypotheses — the\ndegenerate denominators agree on both sides under the field convention. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.qint","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.qint","kind":"def","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/EmCouplingBarParity.lean#L37-L38","doc":"The quantum integer `[n]_q = (qⁿ − q⁻ⁿ)/(q − q⁻¹)`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}